# Automatic UI QA Agent Gate (cookapp) — HARD RULES

Any task that **adds or changes UI** is unfinished until a **separate QA agent** passes. The implementer must not self-approve.

## When to run (mandatory)

After implementing or editing a screen/component, **before** claiming done / final commit message as complete / merge-ready:

1. Commit WIP if needed (so QA has a ref).
2. Dispatch a **fresh** subagent (no implementer chat history) — prefer `computerUse` when the app can run; otherwise `generalPurpose` with screenshot + code paths.
3. QA returns **PASS** or **FAIL** with a concrete violation list.
4. On **FAIL**: treat as rejected — fix or revert the UI delta, then re-run QA. Loop until PASS.
5. On **PASS**: only then mark the UI task complete.

Do **not** skip QA because “it looks fine,” time pressure, or small diffs. No UI change is too small.

## QA agent brief (required prompt contents)

Give the QA agent:

- Screen name(s) and paths to matching files in `docs/ui-screenshots/`
- Paths to changed UI code / running URL if available
- Rules to enforce:
  - `.cursor/rules/ui-screenshots.mdc` (ignore status bar, Dynamic Island, keyboard)
  - `.cursor/rules/ui-fidelity.mdc` (1:1 screenshot)
  - `.cursor/rules/ui-consistency-lock.mdc` (tokens + shared kit, no forks)
  - `.cursor/rules/liquid-glass.mdc` (Liquid Glass chrome only on nav layer; light+dark; control states)

Ask for this exact verdict shape:

```
VERDICT: PASS | FAIL
Screenshot fidelity: ...
Liquid Glass: ...
Consistency (shared chrome/tokens): ...
Control states: ...
Violations: (numbered, actionable)
Required redo: (what to change or revert)
```

## Reject / redo policy

- **FAIL** ⇒ UI is **not accepted**. Either:
  - **Redo**: patch to satisfy every violation, or
  - **Withdraw**: `git revert` / restore prior good UI for the offending files, then redo cleanly.
- Do not merge “temporary” UI that failed QA.
- Do not open new feature UI work on top of a failed screen.
- Re-run the same QA brief after fixes until **PASS**.

## Parallelism

- Implementer agent ≠ QA agent (always separate Task/subagent).
- For multiple screens, one QA pass per screen (or batched with per-screen verdicts); any single FAIL blocks completion of that screen.

## Evidence

QA should compare live UI (or captured frames) to `docs/ui-screenshots/`, ignoring device chrome. If the app cannot run yet, QA reviews code + static composition against screenshots and Liquid Glass rules and still returns PASS/FAIL (FAIL if insufficient evidence of glass/tokens/shared kit).
